Design notes:

- The method uses `Database.insert(toInsert, false)` so partial success is allowed, and it is the only DML statement per call.
- Duplicate detection runs first, over the whole input. The first lead with a given normalized email is kept and every later one is flagged. This holds even if the first lead later fails to insert.
- Only non-duplicate leads go into `toInsert`. I track each one's original index so the save results map back to input positions.
- `insertedIds` lists Ids in input order. Because `toInsert` preserves input order, iterating the save results in order yields that order.
- Database errors are joined with `; `, using `getMessage()` for each error.
- The class uses `with sharing`.
- `LeadSource` defaults to `Web` only on leads that are inserted. Setting it on duplicates is harmless, but I apply it just before insert to be safe.
- Null elements in the list: a null lead can't be inserted, so I record an error for it rather than throwing.
- Email normalization is `trim().toLowerCase()`. A blank email after trimming means the lead is not a duplicate candidate.

```apex
public with sharing class LeadImportService {

    public class ImportResult {
        public Integer successCount = 0;
        public List<Id> insertedIds = new List<Id>();
        public Map<Integer, String> errorsByIndex = new Map<Integer, String>();
    }

    public static ImportResult importLeads(List<Lead> leads) {
        ImportResult result = new ImportResult();
        if (leads == null || leads.isEmpty()) {
            return result;
        }

        List<Lead> toInsert = new List<Lead>();
        List<Integer> indexes = new List<Integer>();
        Set<String> seenEmails = new Set<String>();

        for (Integer i = 0; i < leads.size(); i++) {
            Lead l = leads[i];
            if (l == null) {
                result.errorsByIndex.put(i, 'Lead record is null');
                continue;
            }
            if (String.isNotBlank(l.Email)) {
                String key = l.Email.trim().toLowerCase();
                if (String.isNotBlank(key)) {
                    if (seenEmails.contains(key)) {
                        result.errorsByIndex.put(i, 'Duplicate email in import: ' + key);
                        continue;
                    }
                    seenEmails.add(key);
                }
            }
            if (String.isBlank(l.LeadSource)) {
                l.LeadSource = 'Web';
            }
            toInsert.add(l);
            indexes.add(i);
        }

        if (toInsert.isEmpty()) {
            return result;
        }

        List<Database.SaveResult> saveResults = Database.insert(toInsert, false);
        for (Integer j = 0; j < saveResults.size(); j++) {
            Database.SaveResult sr = saveResults[j];
            if (sr.isSuccess()) {
                result.successCount++;
                result.insertedIds.add(sr.getId());
            } else {
                List<String> msgs = new List<String>();
                for (Database.Error err : sr.getErrors()) {
                    msgs.add(err.getMessage());
                }
                result.errorsByIndex.put(indexes[j], String.join(msgs, '; '));
            }
        }
        return result;
    }
}
