Key LWC concern: element ids in templates are mangled at render time, so a static `id` in the template can't be referenced by a hardcoded `aria-controls` string. Cross-reference ARIA attributes in LWC generally break across template boundaries, but here both elements are in the same template. LWC rewrites `id` values to unique ones (e.g. `section-body-12`) and rewrites static `aria-controls` references in the same template accordingly. However, a dynamic `aria-controls` binding isn't rewritten, so I use a static string that matches the static `id`.

Because the slotted title lives in a native `<button>`, the button's accessible name comes from the slot content. The `hidden` attribute is bound to a boolean getter, so it appears only while collapsed.

