This is the key design question for the NPSP Household Account model: if you insert a Contact with no AccountId, NPSP's trigger (the Account Model "Individual" processing) automatically creates a new household account for each contact. Since we want one household, we have to avoid that.

The approach is to insert the Account first with the Household Account record type, with no Name set. NPSP's household naming only works after contacts exist, and Account.Name is required. NPSP normally handles an empty Name by setting a default on insert, which is why we must not set the name ourselves. Under the Household Account model, inserting an Account with the HH_Account record type is accepted without a name only if a trigger fills it in, and in practice NPSP assigns a name from the contacts. Therefore I create the Account with the record type only, then insert the contacts with AccountId pointing to it. Because the contacts have an AccountId, NPSP won't create individual or extra accounts.

Next, I set `npe01__One2OneContact__c` on the account to the first contact after insert, and update the account. NPSP's household naming then runs from the contact inserts and generates the name and greetings.

The record type Id is resolved dynamically with `Schema.SObjectType.Account.getRecordTypeInfosByDeveloperName().get('HH_Account').getRecordTypeId()`.

For safety, the DML is wrapped with a savepoint so that if the contact insert or the account update fails, the account is rolled back and no extra account is left behind.

The contacts passed in are cloned? No, they're the caller's own records, so I set AccountId on them directly and the caller sees the Ids after insert.

```apex
public with sharing class HouseholdService {

    public static Id createHousehold(List<Contact> members) {
        if (members == null || members.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException('members must contain at least one Contact.');
        }
        for (Contact c : members) {
            if (c == null) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException('members must not contain null entries.');
            }
        }

        Schema.RecordTypeInfo rtInfo = Schema.SObjectType.Account
            .getRecordTypeInfosByDeveloperName().get('HH_Account');
        if (rtInfo == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException('Household Account record type (HH_Account) not found.');
        }

        Savepoint sp = Database.setSavepoint();
        try {
            // Name is intentionally not set; NPSP household naming populates it.
            Account household = new Account(RecordTypeId = rtInfo.getRecordTypeId());
            insert household;

            for (Contact c : members) {
                c.AccountId = household.Id;
            }
            insert members;

            household.npe01__One2OneContact__c = members[0].Id;
            update household;

            return household.Id;
        } catch (Exception e) {
            Database.rollback(sp);
            throw e;
        }
    }
}
