The class implements both `BeforeInsert` and `BeforeUpdate`. It queries once and compares emails case-insensitively. I made these design choices:

- **Which contacts are checked:** on update, only records whose `Email` or `AccountId` changed. Contacts without an Account or Email are skipped.
- **Single query:** it fetches contacts for the candidate accounts whose `Email` is in the candidate set. SOQL `=` and `IN` on text are case-insensitive, so `Email IN :emails` finds case variants. The query is also filtered by `AccountId IN :accountIds`. This can pull extra rows from the cross product of accounts and emails, so each row is still matched on the exact (account, lowercased email) key.
- **Self-conflict:** existing records with an Id in `Trigger.new` are excluded from the query (`Id NOT IN :ids`), so a contact never conflicts with itself. A contact in the same batch that is not being checked, such as an unchanged legacy duplicate, still counts as an existing record. Since it is in `Trigger.new`, the query excludes it, so it must be handled in memory instead.
- **In-batch ordering:** I handle this by registering the keys of every non-checked contact in the batch (those with Account and Email) as "taken". I do not register those that are checked and rejected, because a rejected record doesn't persist. The input is iterated in order. A checked record is rejected if its key is already taken, whether by a DB record or by an earlier accepted record.
- **Unchanged batch records on update:** these are persisted with their current values. Their keys are taken from the new values, which equal the old ones. I seed them into the taken set first. This gives the right result: an edited contact conflicts with an unchanged sibling in the same save. Registering them first is order-independent, which is correct because they already exist.
- **Updated records that are checked:** a record in the batch whose key changed leaves its old key. Using only new values for batch records is correct, since the DB query excludes batch Ids.
- **Partial saves:** `addError` on individual records works with `allOrNone=false`.
- **Rows in the DB side:** the query uses `Id NOT IN :batchIds`. For insert, Ids are null, so I only add non-null Ids.

```apex
public with sharing class TA_Contact_PreventDuplicateEmail implements TriggerAction.BeforeInsert, TriggerAction.BeforeUpdate {
    private static final String ERROR_MESSAGE = 'Another contact on this account already uses this email address.';

    public void beforeInsert(List<SObject> triggerNew) {
        check((List<Contact>) triggerNew, null);
    }

    public void beforeUpdate(List<SObject> triggerNew, List<SObject> triggerOld) {
        Map<Id, Contact> oldMap = new Map<Id, Contact>();
        for (SObject o : triggerOld) {
            oldMap.put(o.Id, (Contact) o);
        }
        check((List<Contact>) triggerNew, oldMap);
    }

    private static String key(Id accountId, String email) {
        return String.valueOf(accountId) + '|' + email.toLowerCase();
    }

    private static void check(List<Contact> newList, Map<Id, Contact> oldMap) {
        Set<String> taken = new Set<String>();
        List<Contact> toCheck = new List<Contact>();
        Set<Id> accountIds = new Set<Id>();
        Set<String> emails = new Set<String>();
        Set<Id> batchIds = new Set<Id>();

        for (Contact c : newList) {
            if (c.Id != null) {
                batchIds.add(c.Id);
            }
            if (c.AccountId == null || String.isBlank(c.Email)) {
                continue;
            }
            Boolean needsCheck = true;
            if (oldMap != null) {
                Contact old = oldMap.get(c.Id);
                if (old != null && old.Email == c.Email && old.AccountId == c.AccountId) {
                    needsCheck = false;
                }
            }
            if (needsCheck) {
                toCheck.add(c);
                accountIds.add(c.AccountId);
                emails.add(c.Email);
            } else {
                taken.add(key(c.AccountId, c.Email));
            }
        }

        if (toCheck.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        for (Contact existing : [
            SELECT AccountId, Email
            FROM Contact
            WHERE AccountId IN :accountIds
            AND Email IN :emails
            AND Id NOT IN :batchIds
        ]) {
            if (existing.AccountId != null && existing.Email != null) {
                taken.add(key(existing.AccountId, existing.Email));
            }
        }

        for (Contact c : toCheck) {
            String k = key(c.AccountId, c.Email);
            if (taken.contains(k)) {
                c.addError(ERROR_MESSAGE);
            } else {
                taken.add(k);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

